## Overview

This is the production-grade Helm sub-chart for the EFE Phase-2 meta-swarm
(controller + N participants).  Disabled by default ; set
`efe-meta-swarm.enabled=true` on the umbrella `efe-stack` chart to bring up
1 controller + N participants (default = 3 Kovant scenarios).

PR #14 layered on top of PR #13's skeleton :
  - multi-environment values flavors (`examples/values-{dev,staging,prod,canary}.yaml`)
  - Helm pre-upgrade snapshot hook + post-upgrade SIGHUP-all hook
  - PrometheusRule alerts (6 alerts across 3 groups)
  - Grafana dashboard ConfigMap (sidecar auto-import via `grafana_dashboard: "1"` label)
  - controller PriorityClass + HPA Phase-2 placeholder (`min=max=1`)
  - bundle weight-loader sidecar (Phase-2 `pause:3.9` placeholder ; PR #15+ swaps for real binary)
  - cert-manager TLS bootstrap stubs (Issuer + per-pod Certificate)
  - per-tenant label propagation + multi-tenant slices

PR #15 added the `helm-meta-swarm-lint` workflow with 14 stages of automated
correctness checks ; see `docs/EFE_A1_PHASE2_PR15_ARCHITECTURE.md`.

PR #16 — production-grade mutual TLS (rustls, cert-manager, inotify rotation,
4 TLS metrics + 3 alerts).

PR #17 — 14 operational Prometheus metrics + 5 PrometheusRule alerts +
cardinality circuit-breaker + PII redaction.  STABILITY_CONTRACT v1.0.

PR #18 — 8 OpenTelemetry span types, W3C trace context propagation,
OTLP/gRPC exporter, 3 exporter health metrics, 3 PrometheusRule alerts.

PR #19 — 9 Grafana dashboards, 10 PrometheusRule alerts, 6 recording rules,
4 SLOs, Alertmanager routing CRD with 3-branch fan-out (PagerDuty / Slack /
Loki audit), 10 operator runbooks.  STABILITY_CONTRACT v1.1 (Dashboard UID /
Alert name / Recording rule name / SLO target tiers).

---

## PR #19 surface — Grafana dashboards + Prometheus alerts + SLOs

| Surface | Files / template | Default knob |
|---|---|---|
| **9 dashboards** (sidecar-discovered) | `files/dashboards/pr19/*.json` → `templates/pr19-dashboards-configmap.yaml` | `dashboard.enabled=true` + `dashboard.pr19.enabled=true` |
| **10 alerts + 6 recording rules** | `templates/pr19-prometheusrule.yaml` | `alerts.enabled=true` + `alerts.pr19.enabled=true` |
| **Alertmanager routing** (CRD) | `templates/pr19-alertmanager-routing-configmap.yaml` | `alerts.pr19.alertmanager.enabled=true` |

### Dashboards UIDs (STABILITY_CONTRACT v1.1 — frozen for 6 minor versions)

| UID | Audience | Default range |
|---|---|---|
| `efe-msw-overview` | On-call SRE | 6h |
| `efe-msw-iterate` | Dev, SRE | 1h |
| `efe-msw-participant` | Dev, SRE | 1h |
| `efe-msw-reload` | SRE, dev | 24h |
| `efe-msw-otel` | SRE | 1h |
| `efe-msw-tls` | SRE, security | 24h |
| `efe-msw-safety` | SRE, dev, compliance | 24h |
| `efe-msw-runtime` | SRE | 1h |
| `efe-msw-traces` | Dev | 15m |

### Alerts (STABILITY_CONTRACT v1.1 — frozen alert names + runbook IDs)

| Alert | Severity | Runbook | SLO |
|---|---|---|---|
| `IterateFailureRateHigh`     | critical | [MSW1](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW1.md)  | — (symptom) |
| `IterateLatencyP99Critical`  | critical | [MSW2](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW2.md)  | iterate-latency-p95 |
| `ParticipantDown`            | warning  | [MSW3](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW3.md)  | — |
| `TLSCertExpiringSoon`        | warning  | [MSW4](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW4.md)  | — |
| `ControllerNotServing`       | critical | [MSW5](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW5.md)  | — (platform) |
| `OTelExporterFailing`        | warning  | [MSW6](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW6.md)  | otel-drop-rate |
| `SafetyViolationSpike`       | warning  | [MSW7](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW7.md)  | — |
| `ManifestReloadFailureSpike` | warning  | [MSW8](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW8.md)  | manifest-reload-latency |
| `SLOBudgetBurnFast14x`       | critical | [MSW9](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW9.md)  | iterate-availability |
| `SLOBudgetBurnSlow6x`        | warning  | [MSW10](../../../../docs/runbooks/RB_PR19_MSW10.md) | iterate-availability |

### SLOs (STABILITY_CONTRACT v1.1 — relaxing a target is a contract break)

| SLO id | Default target | Operator override |
|---|---|---|
| `iterate-availability`         | 99.9 %    | `alerts.pr19.slo.iterateAvailabilityTarget` |
| `iterate-latency-p95`          | ≤ 1.0 s   | `alerts.pr19.slo.iterateLatencyP95Target` |
| `manifest-reload-latency-p95`  | ≤ 0.5 s   | `alerts.pr19.slo.manifestReloadP95Target` |
| `otel-drop-rate`               | ≤ 1.0 %   | `alerts.pr19.slo.otelDropRateTarget` |

### Enabling the PR #19 surface

```bash
helm upgrade efe-meta-swarm ./charts/efe-stack/charts/efe-meta-swarm \
    --set enabled=true \
    --set alerts.enabled=true \
    --set alerts.pr19.enabled=true \
    --set alerts.pr19.alertmanager.enabled=true \
    --set dashboard.enabled=true \
    --set dashboard.pr19.enabled=true \
    --set image.tag=0.6.1
```

Or in `values.yaml` (recommended for prod) :

```yaml
alerts:
  enabled: true
  pr19:
    enabled: true
    slo:
      iterateAvailabilityTarget: 0.999    # 99.9 %
      iterateLatencyP95Target:   1.0      # seconds
      manifestReloadP95Target:   0.5      # seconds
      otelDropRateTarget:        0.01     # 1 %
    alertmanager:
      enabled: true
      mode: alertmanagerconfig
      pagerduty: { secretName: alertmanager-pagerduty-meta-swarm, routingKeyKey: routing-key }
      slack:     { secretName: alertmanager-slack-meta-swarm, urlKey: webhook-url, channel: "#meta-swarm-alerts" }
      audit:     { lokiUrl: "http://loki-gateway.monitoring.svc:3100/audit/alerts" }
dashboard:
  enabled: true
  pr19:
    enabled: true
    datasources:
      prometheusUid: prometheus
      tempoUid:      tempo-efe
```

### Selective rollout

Each surface is independently togglable :

```bash
# Dashboards only (no alerts)
helm upgrade ... --set dashboard.pr19.enabled=true --set alerts.pr19.enabled=false

# Alerts only (no dashboards)
helm upgrade ... --set alerts.pr19.enabled=true --set dashboard.pr19.enabled=false

# Disable just the SLO burn alerts (keep cause/symptom alerts)
helm upgrade ... --set alerts.pr19.enabled=true \
    --set alerts.pr19.slo.iterateAvailabilityTarget=0.0  # disables burn math
```

### External dependencies

- Prometheus must enable exemplar storage for D2 P8 / D3 P5 click-to-trace
  to work (cluster-side : `--enable-feature=exemplar-storage` on the
  Prometheus binary, default in kube-prometheus-stack 0.55+).
- A Tempo datasource must exist in Grafana with UID `tempo-efe` (override
  via `dashboard.pr19.datasources.tempoUid` if your cluster uses a
  different UID).
- A PagerDuty + Slack Secret must pre-exist in the cluster Alertmanager
  namespace (see `alerts.pr19.alertmanager.{pagerduty,slack}.secretName`).

