## Quick start

```bash
# 1. Disabled-by-default render (zero K8s objects) :
helm template tst ./charts/efe-stack/charts/efe-meta-swarm

# 2. Default 3-participant Kovant scenario :
helm install tst ./charts/efe-stack/charts/efe-meta-swarm \
    --namespace efe --create-namespace \
    --set enabled=true \
    --set image.tag=0.3.0

# 3. Production overlay (PriorityClass + alerts + dashboard + hooks + NetworkPolicy) :
helm install tst ./charts/efe-stack/charts/efe-meta-swarm \
    --namespace efe --create-namespace \
    -f ./charts/efe-stack/charts/efe-meta-swarm/examples/values-prod.yaml \
    --set image.tag=0.3.0
```

## SIGHUP-driven reload (PR #12)

```bash
# Edit manifest, then rerun helm upgrade.  The post-upgrade hook
# delivers SIGHUP automatically (if hooks.enabled : true).
helm upgrade tst ./charts/efe-stack/charts/efe-meta-swarm \
    -f my-values.yaml
```

If you need to trigger SIGHUP manually (operator runbook §41 of PR #13) :

```bash
kubectl -n efe exec deploy/tst-efe-meta-swarm-controller -- kill -HUP 1
for p in supplier-scoring contract-risk spend-categorization ; do
    kubectl -n efe exec "deploy/tst-efe-meta-swarm-participant-${p}" -- kill -HUP 1
done
```

